<BaseLayout
  title="About OnDutyCal"
  description="Why OnDutyCal exists: personalized shift calendars for US rotating-shift workers — nurses, firefighters, police, and plant crews — with holidays, paydays, and phone export."
>
  <h1>About OnDutyCal</h1>
  <p>
    OnDutyCal answers one question — <em>"am I working that day?"</em> — for the millions of
    Americans whose work weeks do not repeat weekly. If you rotate on a 2-2-3, Pitman, DuPont,
    4-on-4-off, 48/96, Kelly, or a department calendar like Houston Fire's, your schedule is
    perfectly predictable and completely impossible to eyeball. This site does the modular
    arithmetic: one known workday in, a personalized 12-month calendar out, with every US federal
    holiday answered, paydays marked, and a one-tap export to your phone.
  </p>
  <h2>Principles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Private by architecture.</strong> Every calculation runs in your browser. There are
      no accounts, and your dates are never transmitted or stored on a server.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Sourced, not guessed.</strong> Department-anchored calendars cite the official
      published rotation they are aligned to, and pattern math is cross-checked against public
      department calendars.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fast and free.</strong> Static pages, no app install, no paywall. The site is
      supported by advertising.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    Rotations occasionally change by contract or department decision. Always verify critical dates
    (payroll disputes, leave requests) against your employer's official schedule — OnDutyCal is a
    planning tool, not a payroll document. Found a discrepancy? Please
    <a href="/contact">report it</a>; corrections ship quickly.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
